  "equipment_type": "VRF / split AC gateway",
  "applies_to": "Samsung indoor units on the F3F4 remote-controller bus, gateway set to Modbus RTU (SW1-5 ON); user manual version 1.0.0.",
  "summary": "Dual-protocol gateway (BACnet MS/TP or Modbus RTU, chosen by DIP switch) for Samsung air conditioners on the F3F4 remote-controller bus. In Modbus mode, holding registers cover on/off, mode, fan, vanes, setpoints including dual setpoint, thermistor input, window contact logic, filter status, WindFree/AirClean, errors and firmware version.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": 2400,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "Tables give 'Modbus address (base 0)' and 'PLC address (base 1)'; the base-0 address is the wire address and is used for 'documented'."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "IN485SAM001R000 User Manual",
    "doc_number": "User Manual Version 1.0.0",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.hms-networks.com/docs/default-source/products/intesis/manuals-and-guides---manuals/user-manual-in485sam001r000.pdf",
    "pages": "pp. 8-10 (DIP switches), p. 21 (functions, physical layer), pp. 22-27 (registers)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Temperatures can be set to °C, °C x10, °F or °F x10 with SW2-7/8; factory default is whole °C (x1). Temperature registers are listed as signed INT16 because the manual prints the no-value marker as 0x8000 (-32768).",
    "The gateway ships set for BACnet MS/TP; SW1-5 must be ON for Modbus RTU. In Modbus mode the default baud rate is 2400 bps.",
    "FC16 is accepted only with a length of 1 register.",
    "Left out: machine minimum/maximum setpoint registers 1153-1156, because their scale (x1/x10) is not stated. The 'characterization bitfield' tables are not mapped because the manual does not tie them to Modbus addresses.",
    "Error code list not reproduced; see the manual's error-code section."
  ],
